{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788049920374498670,"compiled_state":{"alias":"miserable-pernickety-caudata","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b51c651701e4e3e26be75aade00176d4fe32c78873e0ac8ad4eec118d71ab852","event_uuid":"8a3884c9-a8be-4019-b173-8595e8ee14a3","position":{"commit_sha":"2883f7005796ee63bdbaecf2e50dec1c87916c62","position":"1788046542480098623-8a3884c9-a8be-4019-b173-8595e8ee14a3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788046542480098623,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\nThe `tickets` pack grows ~2.0 KiB/commit at ~14K commits/day because each enrichment step\n(ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE_ENRICH) and each `TICKET_DIGEST` is written as its OWN commit, re-emitting the\n270 KB root tree every time. Below-horizon collapse (S1) removes the historical churn; W1 removes\nthe churn AT THE SOURCE so it does not re-accumulate, which is what keeps the pack under budget\nafter the reclaim lands.\n\n## Scope\n\nBatch the derived enrichment quartet + digest for a single logical mutation into ONE write/commit\n(one root-tree re-emission) instead of 3-4, without changing observable ticket state, event\nsemantics, signatures, or optimistic-concurrency guarantees. Preserve per-event signing/verifiability.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe history reclaim of already-accumulated commits (that is S1). No change to the event schema's\nobservable contract beyond commit batching.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A single logical mutation that today emits the enrichment quartet + digest as separate commits emits ONE commit (one root-tree re-emission), measured on a fixture.\n- [ ] Observable reduced ticket state is unchanged vs the pre-batch behavior (reducer-equality fixture passes).\n- [ ] Each batched event retains its individual signature and passes `rebar verify-authorship`.\n- [ ] Optimistic-concurrency / audit guarantees are preserved (existing concurrency tests pass).\n- [ ] The measured commits-per-mutation and per-mutation root-tree re-emission count drop as designed.\n\n## Portability\n\nPure library/store change; no dependence on any single CI provider.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6816-69bf-460d-4db1","ticket_type":"task","title":"W1: batch enrichment quartet + digest into one write lane (cut ~14K commits/day at source)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8a3884c9-a8be-4019-b173-8595e8ee14a3"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788049920374498670,"uuid":"dcfeb1a7-492a-4343-b1fc-4dbf52641bdb"}